      "writtenOn": "2024-12-17T20:36:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why dont we account for the conn_state-\u003emin_requested_bpc here?, dfp.min_bpc is set to 0, does it get updated to conn_state-\u003emin_requested_bpc somewhere? This is what gets propagated to limits-\u003epipe.min_bpp so we need to account for the minbpc somewhere so that it gets reflected in the limits-\u003epipe.min_bpp",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1108,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1108,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "01005c77840f3340455b07b2e51e674c7a764f6e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c8295296_86bbc5a4",
        "filename": "drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 1108,
      "author": {
        "id": 3593604
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-18T18:27:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We account for `conn_state-\u003emin_requested_bpc` in `intel_dp_dsc_mst_compute_link_config` when we check `limits-\u003epipe.min_bpp`.\n\n`limits-\u003epipe.max_bpp` does not seem to use `conn_state-\u003emax_requested_bpc` either?",
      "parentUuid": "de791be6_f8fda6f6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1108,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1108,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "01005c77840f3340455b07b2e51e674c7a764f6e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ae755b9a_f84593a8",
        "filename": "drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 1108,
      "author": {
        "id": 3515397
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-18T20:47:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "limits-\u003epipe.max_bpp does not need to look at the max_requested_bpc , it derives it from crtc_state-\u003epipe_bpp and that is computed in compute_pipe_sink_bpp that makes sure that its within the conn_state-\u003emax_bpc range. Whereas limits-\u003epipe.min_bpp is computed using intel_dp_min_bpp so thats where we should check for conn_state--\u003erequested_min_bpc and ensure the min is that. Since limits-\u003epipe.min_bpp will then be used in intel_dp_compute_link_config_wide() to determine link rate lane count by reducing the bpc to min of limits-\u003epipe.min_bpp.  This will determine if for that min requested bpp are the link rate/lane count enough or does it need dsc, if it does then it will check the min bpp and max bpp with DSC in intel_dp_dsc_compute_config .",
      "parentUuid": "c8295296_86bbc5a4",
